.TH CI_GET_SERVERS 3 "5 March 2010"
.SH NAME
ci_get_servers, ci_get_servers_ports \- Retrieve name servers from an initialized ci_channel (deprecated)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ci.h>

int ci_get_servers(const ci_channel_t *\fIchannel\fP,
                     struct ci_addr_node **\fIservers\fP)

int ci_get_servers_ports(const ci_channel_t *\fIchannel\fP,
                           struct ci_addr_port_node **\fIservers\fP)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBci_get_servers(3)\fP function retrieves name servers configuration
from the
channel data identified by
.IR channel ,
as a linked list of ci_addr_node structs storing a pointer to the first
node at the address specified by
.IR servers .

The \fBci_get_servers_ports(3)\fP function also retrieves any per-server
port information that may have been previously configured, returning a linked
list of ci_addr_port structures.

Function caller may traverse the returned name server linked list, or may use
it directly as suitable input for the \fBci_set_servers(3)\fP /
\fBci_set_servers_ports(3)\fP functions, but
shall not shrink or extend the list on its own.

Each node of the name server linked list is stored in memory dynamically
allocated and managed by c-ci. It is the caller's responsibility to free
the resulting linked list, using \fBci_free_data(3)\fP , once the caller
does not need it any longer.

This function is capable of handling IPv4 and IPv6 name server
addresses simultaneously, rendering \fBci_save_options(3)\fP with
optmask \fBCI_OPT_SERVERS\fP functionally obsolete except for
IPv4-only name server usage.

.SH RETURN VALUES
This function may return any of the following values:
.TP 15
.B CI_SUCCESS
The name servers configuration was successfully retrieved
.TP 15
.B CI_ENOMEM
The memory was exhausted
.TP 15
.B CI_ENODATA
The channel data identified by
.IR channel
was invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ci_set_servers (3),
.BR ci_init_options (3),
.BR ci_save_options(3)
.SH AVAILABILITY
\fBci_get_servers(3)\fP was added in c-ci 1.7.1;
\fBci_get_servers_ports(3)\fP was added in c-ci 1.11.0.
.SH NOTES
As of c-ci 1.24, these functions are deprecated due to their lack of ability
to store the entire server configuration.  Use \fBci_get_servers_csv(3)\fP.
